window.docContents[252].resolve({"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Geometry/#LindenstraussPolynomials___geometry_lemma":{"contents":"Lemma lem:geometry. Let a be a symmetric (d+1)-linear form (the symmetric form of\nP), ‖P‖ ≤ M, u₀,…,u_d ∈ B_X, f₀,…,f_{d-1} ∈ B_{X*}, and suppose that\nRe P(S₀(t₀) ⋯ S_{d-1}(t_{d-1}) u_d) ≥ M - E for all tᵢ ∈ [0,1].  Then\n|a(u₀,…,u_d)| ≥ M - H_{d+1} √(ME). \n\n","context":"","header":"LindenstraussPolynomials.geometry_lemma","id":"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Geometry/#LindenstraussPolynomials___geometry_lemma"},"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Geometry/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Geometry-1-0":{"contents":"The geometric lemma \\(Lemma lem:geometry and Remark rem:real\\)\n\nLet \\|P\\|\\le M, u_1,\\ldots,u_n in the unit ball of X and f_1,\\ldots,f_{n-1} in the unit ball of X^*. If\n\\operatorname{Re}P\\bigl(S_1(t_1)\\cdots S_{n-1}(t_{n-1})\\,u_n\\bigr)\\ge M-E\\quad\\text{for all }t_1,\\ldots,t_{n-1}\\in[0,1],\nthen the fully mixed value of the symmetric form is almost maximal:\n|\\check P(u_1,\\ldots,u_n)| \\ge M - H_n\\sqrt{ME}.\nOver \\mathbb R the bound improves to M-C_nE (Remark rem:real).\n\n\n","context":"","header":"LindenstraussPolynomials.Geometry","id":"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Geometry/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Geometry-1-0"}});